        engineeringData: { blockDesign: "Inline-6, Open-deck Aluminum block with cast iron cylinder liners. The N55 was designed to be vastly more reliable day-to-day than the high-maintenance N54 it replaced. While the open-deck design is strong, it uses a cast crankshaft and weaker rods than the N54, meaning it cannot handle extreme 600+ hp tuning safely.", crankshaft: "Cast Iron, supported by 7 main bearings. (Early N55s can suffer from rod bearing failures).", pistonSpeed: "15.4 m/s @ 7000 RPM.", alternator: "180A Valeo.", rotatingAssembly: { pistonConstruction: "Cast aluminum alloy. Features a 10.2:1 compression ratio.", wristPinDiameter: "22 mm.", connectingRodLength: "144 mm.", rodBoltSize: "M9.", crankMainJournal: "50.0 mm.", crankRodJournal: "45.0 mm.", rodRatio: "1.61." }, cylinderHead: { combustionChamberVol: "Direct injection specific pent-roof design.", intakePortFlow: "24-valve DOHC design. The N55 crucially added Valvetronic (variable valve lift) acting as the throttle, which the N54 lacked. This vastly improves throttle response and fuel efficiency, but adds a highly complex eccentric shaft that can wear out.", valveSizes: "Intake: 32.0 mm / Exhaust: 28.0 mm.", valveStemDiameter: "5.0 mm.", camshaftDuration: "Highly variable via Double-VANOS and Valvetronic.", lifterType: "Hydraulic bucket tappets.", specialFeature: "Valvetronic, Twin-Scroll Turbo & ZF 8-Speed. The LCI E71 X6 introduced the N55 engine and the groundbreaking ZF 8-speed automatic. The N55 dropped the complex twin turbos in favor of a single Twin-Scroll unit, completely eliminating lag and making the engine much more reliable. Furthermore, it retains the incredible Dynamic Performance Control (DPC) rear torque-vectoring differential." }, oilAndCooling: { oilSquirters: "Yes, under-piston cooling jets.", oilPumpType: "Chain-driven variable displacement map-controlled pump.", thermostatOpening: "Electronically mapped by the ECU (ranges from 90°C to 105°C).", oilCooler: "Standard integrated liquid-to-liquid heat exchanger. (Prone to OFHG leaks)." }, fuelSystem: { systemType: "Bosch High Precision Direct Injection.", maxPressure: "200 Bar (Fuel Rail). The N55 HPFP is significantly more robust than the N54 version.", injectors: "6x Bosch Solenoid Injectors (Vastly more reliable than N54 Piezo units)." }, tuningLimits: { maxSafeTorqueStock: "500 Nm (The ZF 8HP45 transmission is maxed out here).", maxSafePowerStock: "450 hp (The N55 cast crank and weaker rods limit safe tuning compared to the N54).", maxSafeRPM: "7000 RPM", weakestLink: "Charge Pipe (Explodes), Electric Water Pump (Sudden failure), OFHG Oil Leak (Belt Ingestion), Rod Bearings (Early models), Valvetronic." }, electrical: { coils: "Individual Coil Pack system (Bosch/Eldor).", ecu: "Bosch MEVD17.2 (Highly tunable and deeply mapped by the aftermarket community)." } },
