        sisterModels: [ { name: "BMW 550i (F10 CN Spec)", note: "The Chinese market F10 550i utilized the exact same artificially restricted N63 V8 engine. The immense DIY knowledge base regarding valve stem seals, Hot-V coolant lines, and injector upgrades translates perfectly to this X6." } ],
        tuningPotential: [
          { stage: "Stage 1 (Bootmod3 / MHD Flash)", power: "480 - 500 hp", notes: "THE ULTIMATE SLEEPER UPGRADE. An OBD software flash safely bypasses the artificial restriction, unlocking a terrifying amount of power from the twin-turbo V8. It jumps from a restricted 349hp to roughly 500hp and 750Nm of torque. The factory ZF 6-speed transmission handles this effortlessly. It turns the heavy X6 into a genuine supercar killer. Note: ONLY DO THIS AFTER FULLY BULLETPROOFING THE ENGINE.", zeroToHundred: "4.8s", hundredToTwoHundred: "11.5s" },
          { stage: "Stage 2 (Downpipes & Tune)", power: "530 - 550 hp", notes: "Requires high-flow or catless downpipes and an aggressive tune. The exhaust note becomes incredibly violent. Due to the high heat of the Hot-V, EGTs must be heavily monitored. The N63 block handles this well, but it pushes the fragile cooling system to its absolute limits.", zeroToHundred: "4.5s", hundredToTwoHundred: "10.5s" },
          { stage: "Stage 3 (Upgraded Turbos)", power: "600 - 650+ hp", notes: "Requires upgrading the factory Garrett turbos to hybrid units. While the N63 block can technically make this power, it is a ticking time bomb. The sheer amount of heat generated will melt every plastic component under the hood and snap the weak timing chains. Only for extreme risk-takers.", zeroToHundred: "4.0s", hundredToTwoHundred: "9.0s" }
        ],
